---An `ObjStackEntity` represents an collection of individual ObjEntry instances that are currently on a tile in the
---game world.
---
---See ObjStackList for information on how to access `ObjStackEntities`.
---
---Info: An `ObjStackEntity` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Warning: Use `ObjStackEntity.isValid` to confirm that an entity still exists before trying to access its properties.
---Entities can be removed from the client by the server for various reasons, i.e. due to moving beyond the player view
---distance or death. When an entity is removed it will become invalid, and any copies of this usertype should be
---disposed of. If the same entity is re-added to the client by the server, such as walking back into visibility range,
---then a different new ObjStackEntity will be created.
---
---Information available within an `ObjStackEntity` includes:
---@class ObjStackEntity
---@field isValid boolean (Read-only) Whether this entity still exists. Dispose of this usertype object when invalid.
---@field position Vector3 (Read-only) The world position of this `ObjStackEntity`.
---@field coordGrid CoordGrid (Read-only) Returns the CoordGrid tile this `ObjStackEntity` is currently on.
---@field aabb AABB (Read-only) Returns the current bounding box for this `ObjStackEntity`.
---@field stackSize integer (Read-only) The number of ObjEntries in this `ObjStackEntity`.
local ObjStackEntity = {}

---Returns the ObjEntry at the given `index`.
---@param index integer The index of the ObjEntry to return. The value of `index` starts at `1`. Returns `nil` if no entry is found at the given index.
---@return ObjEntry?
function ObjStackEntity:GetEntry(index) end

---Returns whether an ObjStackEntity contains an ObjEntry referencing the given ObjType.
---@param objType ObjType The ObjType to search for.
---@return boolean # Whether the ObjType was found.
function ObjStackEntity:HasObj(objType) end

---Returns whether an ObjStackEntity contains an ObjEntry referencing the given ObjType ID.
---@param objTypeID integer The ID of ObjType to search for.
---@return boolean # Whether the ObjType was found.
function ObjStackEntity:HasObjID(objTypeID) end

---Every `ObjStackEntity` contains one or more instances of `ObjEntry`. Each `ObjEntry` references a single ObjType
---config and a count of how many there are.
---
---Info: For objects that cannot stack, like logs, there will be a separate entry for each one. For stackable objects,
---like arrowheads, there will be a single entry with a total count of how many there are. Stackable objects do not
---merge. If another object of the same stackable type was dropped into the stack, it will remain a separate object.
---@class ObjEntry
---@field config ObjType (Read-only) The config that describes this entry.
---@field configID integer (Read-only) The config ID that describes this entry.
---@field count integer (Read-only) How many of this object are in this specific entry. This will always be `1` for ObjTypes that cannot stack.
